# Inventory Management System

A simple command-line inventory management system written in Python. It lets you manage products and keep track of stock levels. Success messages are shown in green and error messages in red.

## Features

- Add, view, search, update and remove products
- Check stock levels and see which products are low on stock (fewer than 5 units)
- Restock a product or reduce its stock
- See the total value of all stock
- Data is saved automatically, so your products are still there next time you run the program
- Colored output using [colorama](https://pypi.org/project/colorama/)

## Requirements

- Python 3
- colorama

## Installation

1. Clone the repository:

       git clone https://github.com/evragitonga/Group3-project-inventory-management-system.git
       cd Group3-project-inventory-management-system

2. Install the required package:

       pip install colorama

## How to Run

    python main.py

You will see a menu. Type the number of the option you want and press Enter:

    1. Add product
    2. View all products
    3. Search for a product
    4. Update a product
    5. Remove a product
    6. Check stock levels
    7. Restock a product
    8. Reduce stock
    9. Total stock value
    0. Exit

Choose 0 to save and exit.

## Project Structure

    main.py        # Menu and program entry point
    models/        # Product and Inventory classes
    data/          # Saving and loading data
    util/          # Helper code

## Colored Output

- Green `[SUCCESS]` messages show that an action worked, for example `[SUCCESS] Product added with ID P1`
- Red `[ERROR]` messages show that something went wrong, for example `[ERROR] Product not found.`

